{"chunk_id": "dd80e10bd765", "text": "Bharata returns to Ayodhya expecting a joyful reunion with his father and brothers but instead finds the city desolate and filled with mourning. Disturbed by the ominous signs, he enters the palace and goes to his mother Kaikeyi\u2019s chamber, where he learns the shocking news that King Dasharatha has died. Overcome with grief, Bharata collapses and laments his father, recalling the king\u2019s affection and wondering why he died without seeing him again. Kaikeyi reveals that Dasharatha died calling out for Rama, Sita, and Lakshmana. When Bharata anxiously asks where Rama is, Kaikeyi discloses that Rama has gone into exile in the Dandaka forest wearing bark garments. The chapter marks the beginning of Bharata\u2019s discovery of the disastrous consequences of Kaikeyi\u2019s ambition, setting up his moral response and the coming conflict over the throne.\nBharata returns to a grief-stricken Ayodhya, learns of King Dasharatha\u2019s death, and hears from Kaikeyi that Rama has been exiled to the forest.\nThemes: grief and mourning, maternal ambition, exile of Rama, filial devotion, fate and duty", "vector": [0.011799031868577003, -0.01406655553728342, -0.009056910872459412, -0.011871539987623692, -0.019168483093380928, 0.01972218044102192, -0.031007064506411552, 0.003533117938786745, -0.020671376958489418, -0.0054941303096711636, 0.020051762461662292, 0.009228292852640152, -0.006637779530137777, 0.025311889126896858, -0.0108893858268857, -0.0005940714036114514, 0.03200899437069893, -0.0038890664000064135, 0.03548938035964966, -0.0129327941685915, 0.011785848997533321, -0.003310650121420622, -0.004943728446960449, 0.019919930025935173, -0.015701280906796455, 0.009432634338736534, 0.018021538853645325, -0.030954333022236824, 0.019273949787020683, -0.01361832395195961, -0.017243724316358566, -0.012306587770581245, -0.0020928450394421816, -0.011113502085208893, -0.0053095645271241665, 0.015793563798069954, -0.012115431018173695, -0.00